    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>A K-nearest-neighbor graph built by NN-descent, with a result that does not depend on the thread count.</para>
<para>Dong, Charikar and Li, &quot;Efficient K-Nearest Neighbor Graph Construction for
Generic Similarity Measures&quot;, WWW 2011. The batch structure follows pyNNDescent in ParlayANN (Manohar et al., PPoPP 2024).</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Initialization: random cluster trees. Each tree splits the points by their nearer of two random pivots, down to leaves of at most 512 points, and links each point to its K nearest in its leaf. With ntrees = 0, each node gets K random neighbors. Rows that stay short get random neighbors.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Rounds: a round reads a fixed copy of the graph. For each node u, a local join computes the distances between the members of the neighborhood of u (its K neighbors and R nearest reverse neighbors), for the pairs where at least one member is new (added by the previous round), and inserts each pair as a candidate in the rows of both members. The new row of a node holds the K best of its old row and of its candidates by (distance, id), with the smallest distance of each id. This set does not depend on the order of the candidates, so the rows do not depend on the thread count.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The vectors are read in place for <ref refid="structfaiss_1_1IndexFlat" kindref="compound">IndexFlat</ref>, decoded for <ref refid="structfaiss_1_1IndexScalarQuantizer" kindref="compound">IndexScalarQuantizer</ref>, and reconstructed for other storage types. The distances of a leaf and of a local join come from the inner products of the float vectors: from the nndescent::gram_upper_rows kernel on AVX2, AVX-512 and ARM NEON or SVE, else from BLAS. The values of a level do not depend on the thread count, but differ between levels. Distances are smaller-is-better: for METRIC_INNER_PRODUCT they are negated inner products. A distance that overflows to NaN becomes +inf. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
